WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.452
On this slide, we are focusing on update a dictionary.

00:00:03.452 --> 00:00:08.262
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.262 --> 00:00:17.107
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:17.412
A dictionary stores key-value pairs.

00:00:17.412 --> 00:00:25.742
Meaningful keys such as name, status, amount, or category make the structure easier to understand than

00:00:25.742 --> 00:00:28.877
position alone. Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:28.877 --> 00:00:35.027
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:35.027 --> 00:00:38.372
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:43.383
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
